# capability_ungranted_use — NEGATIVE test. main declares `effect write
# console.stdout` and performs a write, but `uses` NO capability granting it
# (an uncovered effect, README §8/§12/§17 #5).
#
# Correctness observation (verified):
#   * default `semanticscript check` -> ERROR SS1708 (effect not covered by a capability).
#   * default `semanticscript run`   -> REJECTED before execution by the compile gate.
#   * `semanticscript check --json`  -> nonzero diagnostic envelope.
# This proves the authority model enforces the gap by default.

CapabilityUngrantedUse is project
CapabilityUngrantedUse module examplesCapabilityUngrantedUse
CapabilityUngrantedUse target console
CapabilityUngrantedUse entry main

examplesCapabilityUngrantedUse is module
examplesCapabilityUngrantedUse path examples.capabilityUngrantedUse
examplesCapabilityUngrantedUse exports main
examplesCapabilityUngrantedUse purpose "Write without granting the write capability"
examplesCapabilityUngrantedUse invariant "The write effect is intentionally uncovered"

ExitCode is alias
ExitCode for Int32
ExitCode purpose "Process exit status"

main is operation
main out ExitCode
main effect write console.stdout
main memory heap no
main async no
main purpose "Attempt a write with no capability backing the declared effect"
main invariant "Gate rejects the uncovered write effect"
main let message immutable String "should never print"
main let okCode immutable ExitCode 0
main do writeMsg
main return okCode

writeMsg is call
writeMsg in main
writeMsg invokes console.writeLine
writeMsg arg text String message
